IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `an72-nouns`
IMPORT `an72-cross-references`

-- Row il-72. TESTS OF THE CONTROLS: the sound references kept beside the defects. They pass.
-- Each control is a provision the instruments name that the citing words do not name, a pair of footnotes that identify one ordinance, or a date order. The expected values are hand-written from the quotation lines in an72-cross-references.l4 and from the printed pages, not copied from the statuses there.
-- No assertion here evaluates section 25 of the Interpretation Law; the page facts about it are pinned in an72-tests-readings.l4.

§ `Tests of the controls`

-- ===== I1 =====
-- Section 12(1) of SH 444 repeals section 56 of an ordinance with a different title, which section 27(c) does not name: the test tells the two ordinances apart.
#ASSERT NOT (`Criminal Procedure Ordinance (Evidence)` EQUALS `Criminal Procedure Ordinance (Trial on Indictment)`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the repealed provision reaches the cited provision` `Trial on Indictment section 56` `Evidence section 4`)
#ASSERT NOT (`pointer in section 27(c): section 2`'s `the ordinance the pointer names` EQUALS `Criminal Procedure Ordinance (Trial on Indictment)`)
#ASSERT NOT (`pointer in section 27(c): sections 3 and 4`'s `the ordinance the pointer names` EQUALS `Criminal Procedure Ordinance (Trial on Indictment)`)

-- Sections 2 and 3 are not named by section 12 of SH 444: the test does not flag a section the instrument does not repeal.
#ASSERT NOT (`some listed instruction repeals a provision that reaches the cited provision` `Evidence section 2` `the instructions deposited here`)
#ASSERT NOT (`some listed instruction repeals a provision that reaches the cited provision` `Evidence section 3` `the instructions deposited here`)

-- The footnote of SH 81 page 238 and footnote 6 of SH 444 page 53 name the same place; footnote 5 of SH 444, for the other item, names another.
#ASSERT `the two footnotes name the same place` `footnote 2 of SH 81 page 238` `footnote 6 of SH 444 page 53`
#ASSERT NOT (`the two footnotes name the same place` `footnote 2 of SH 81 page 238` `footnote 5 of SH 444 page 53`)

-- The issue date of SH 81 is earlier than that of SH 444.
#ASSERT `the issue date of SH 81` LESS THAN (`SH 444 section 12 repeals`'s `the issue date its footer prints`)

-- ===== I2 =====
-- A section 10 with a subsection (1) is printed in the 1943 Gazette text.
#ASSERT `the cited provision is among the printed provisions` `Labour Department section 10 (1)` `the provisions printed in the Gazette text`

-- Subsections 4 (2) and 5 (d), also named by section 41(1) of SH 164, are not named by section 27(a): the test counts only what the citing words name.
#ASSERT NOT (`the repealed provision reaches the cited provision` `Labour Department section 4 (2)` `Labour Department section 10 (1)`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the repealed provision reaches the cited provision` `Labour Department section 5 (d)` `Labour Department section 10 (1)`)

-- Section 41(2) names sections of a different ordinance, which section 27(a) does not name.
#ASSERT NOT (`the repealed provision reaches the cited provision` `Factories section 39` `Labour Department section 10 (1)`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the repealed provision reaches the cited provision` `Factories section 40` `Labour Department section 10 (1)`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Labour Department Ordinance, 1943` EQUALS `Factories Ordinance, 1946`)

-- The two footnotes that name the Gazette supplement name the same issue and supplement.
#ASSERT `the two footnotes name the same Gazette issue and supplement` `footnote 1 of SH 81 page 238` `footnote 1 of SH 164 page 208`

-- The issue date of SH 81 is earlier than that of SH 164.
#ASSERT `the issue date of SH 81` LESS THAN (`SH 164 section 41 repeals`'s `the issue date its footer prints`)

-- The day a repeal took effect is not given by the pages read, so there is no answer.
#ASSERT `the day the repeal took effect` `SH 444 section 12 repeals` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the day the repeal took effect` `SH 164 section 41 repeals` EQUALS NOTHING
